S,G|               EXT. OPEN COUNTRY - WIDE ANGLE SHOT - THE POSSE - DUSK
O|
N|               This should be an expansive view to convey the fact that the 
N|               posse has split -- the main group heading for the Jorgensen 
N|               place, Martin forking off to race alone for the Edwards ranch.
O|
N,G|               Coming toward and passing CAMERA is Martin, riding all out.
O|
N|               Several hundred yards away and moving in a divergent direction 
N|               are the others -- Brad and Charlie, Sam, Jorgensen and Ed 
N|               Nesby. The men are not compactly bunched, but strung out, 
N|               each taking his own best course and his own speed... As the 
N,G|               riders pass and the dust of their passing, we see two other 
N|               riders -- Ethan and Mose -- minute specks in the distance, 
N|               possibly a mile or two behind.
O|
S,G|               EXT. OPEN COUNTRY - MOVING SHOT - ETHAN AND MOSE - DUSK
O|
M|               (NOTE TO W. HOCH: What we are trying to get here is that 
M|               moment of swift transition from twilight to night; of riders 
M|               briefly touched with the last colors of day and then, as 
M|               they pass, becoming one with blue shadows of night.)
O|
N|               Ethan and Mose are holding their mounts to a jog, in marked 
N,G|               contrast to the all-out pace of the others. The CAMERA PANS 
N|               after them as the dark fingers of the night stretch across 
N|               the valley. The wind begins to rise and somewhere off in the 
N|               hills a coyote pack yaps.
