S,G|               EXT. RISING GROUND - MED. CLOSE SHOT - MARTIN - MOONLIGHT
O|
N|               He stands beside his spent and fallen horse. Its breathing 
N|               is a rasping whistle. Martin tries to haul its head up.
O|
N|               Useless. Breathing hard himself, his face ashen in the 
N|               moonlight, Martin looks desperately off in the direction of 
N|               the ranch. Then he jerks the rifle from its saddle scabbard -- 
N|               struggling with it because it is under the horse. He freezes 
N|               then -- listening... And we hear the steady beat of two 
N|               horsemen approaching. Martin knows who they are and his face 
N|               is alive with hope. He gets the rifle free at last and goes 
N|               running toward the oncoming riders.
O|
C|                                     MARTIN
P|                              (shouting)
U|                         Ethan!... Ethan!
O|
N,G|               The CAMERA SWINGS with him and we see Ethan and Mose 
N|               approaching at the same steady gait.
O|
C|                                     MARTIN
P|                              (waving)
U|                         Uncle Ethan... it's me... Martin!
O|
N|               Ethan doesn't slacken, nearly rides him down.
O|
C|                                     ETHAN
U|                         Out of my way!
O|
N|               Martin goes sprawling to his hands and knees. Mose continues 
N|               without slowing.
O|
