N,G|               The ANGLE is past the porch uprights toward Mose and Ethan 
N|               as they ride in. Little tongues of fire are licking the edges 
N|               of the uprights. A few arrows, imbedded in the wood, are 
N|               burning along their shafts. Beyond are the glowing ashes of 
N|               the hayricks and the charred, smouldering rails of the corral.
O|
N|               There are no bodies in evidence... The red glow of the burning 
N|               is on the faces of the men as they dismount.
O|
N|               Ethan strides to the porch, knocking away one of the blazing 
N|               arrows as he heads to the door. He stops there -- and what 
N|               he sees makes the big shoulders droop, the huge frame slump.
O|
N|               Slowly then -- and removing his hat -- he goes in. Mose 
N|               shuffles to the edge of the porch and squats there and rocks 
N|               back and forth, his face working and crying soundlessly with 
N|               senile grief. We hear a splintered door crash from its hinges 
N|               within the room and Ethan's muffled voice calling through 
N|               the house:
O|
C,E|                                     ETHAN (O.S.)
U|                         Lucy?... Deborah? Lucy?
O|
