N,I|               range work. One Comanche breaks through from the side, his 
N|               buffalo lance ready for the thrust. Ethan whirls and fires.
O|
N|               The Comanche horse charges through the defense line and out 
N|               and there is a muffled scream of pain from Ed Nesby.
O|
O|               77-C
O|
S,G|               EXT. THE RIVER - WIDE ANGLE - THE INDIANS
O|
N|               The charge breaks and Comanches wheel left and right, racing 
N|               back across the river. With magnificent horsemanship, one 
N,I|               brave rides to an unhorsed warrior crouched in the shallows 
N,I|               and swings him up behind. Two others, riding together, head 
N|               for one of the two dead Comanches Ethan and Mose had downed 
N|               on their first shots. Swinging simultaneously from their 
N|               saddles, they grab the dead man and carry him off.
O|
O|               77-D
O|
S,G|               EXT. THE RIVER'S EDGE - ANGLING PAST MOSE AND ETHAN
O|
C|                                     MOSE
P|                              (cackling)
U|                         There goes yer scalp, Ethan!...
O|
