U|                         Stop it! Both of you... I won't have 
U|                         any fighting in this house.
O|
N|               Martin gently brushes her aside.
O|
C|                                     MARTIN
U|                         It's all right... Charlie, let's 
U|                         move outside.
O|
C|                                     CHARLIE
U|                         I ain't wearing no gun.
O|
N|               Martin nods and unbuckles his gunbelt. The men head outside 
N|               as Laurie runs to get help.
O|
S|               EXT. THE JORGENSEN HOME - BREEZEWAY
O|
N|               Charlie waits assuredly as Martin follows him outside.
O|
N|               Martin makes a wild run, swings. The blow is neatly guarded 
N|               by Charlie's left and countered with a crisp right that puts 
N|               Martin down. Martin gets to his feet, more cautiously this 
N|               time, and comes in at a crouch; he's fighting like an Indian, 
N|               not a white man. The men from the wedding party come out now 
N|               at a run.
O|
C|                                     CLAYTON
P|                              (yelling)
U|                         Sergeant MacCorry!
O|
N|               Charlie turns slightly and in that instant Martin springs 
N|               and drives a straight right at his face -- almost as though 
N|               there were a knife in the hand. MacCorry stumbles back into 
N|               Clayton's arms.
O|
C|                                     CLAYTON
U|                         Is this in the line of duty, sergeant?
O|
C|                                     CHARLIE
P|                              (regaining his balance)
U|                         No sir... pleasure.
O|
C|                                     CLAYTON
U|                         In that case, give the boys room...
O|
N|               Martin waits at a crouch as Charlie comes in, feints his 
N|               right and crosses his left. It is a hard blow but Martin 
N|               recovers and waits... Charlie circles and starts to repeat. 
N|               He feints his right but this time Martin springs in, ducks 
N|               and -- as the left shoots out -- he grabs the wrist and throws 
N|               Charlie over his head. What we are looking at, in effect, is 
N|               a wrestler against a boxer.
O|
C|                                     CLAYTON
U|                         Fight fair, son... Use your fists!
O|
C|                                     ETHAN
P|                              (drily)
U|                         Comanches don't use their fists, 
U|                         reverend... Let 'em alone...
O|
N|               Charlie is on his feet and warily starts circling -- now 
N|               trying to imitate Martin's crouch. Suddenly Martin feints a 
N|               right swing and connects with a solid left -- reversing the 
N|               order of business. Charlie staggers and Martin follows up 
N|               with a wrestling hold, leaping behind Charlie, locking both 
N|               legs around him and driving his arms upward behind his back 
N|               so that his face is in the dirt and so he could -- under 
N|               other circumstances -- be neatly and expeditiously scalped. 
N|               With the hands locked, Martin then calmly draws a knife. He 
N|               looks innocently into the aghast faces of the crowd.
O|
C|                                     MARTIN
U|                         Could scalp him... but I'll just 
U|                         count coup!
O|
N|               With that he releases the paralyzed arms just long enough to 
N|               grab a lock of Charlie's hair and neatly snip it off.
O|
N|               He stands then and laughs as Charlie lamely gets to his feet -- 
N|               easing the tortured arms. Clayton goes to Charlie's side. 
N|               Laurie moves to Martin's side.
O|
C|                                     CLAYTON
U|                         You all right, sergeant?
O|
C|                                     CHARLIE
U|                         Dunno... Seems so.
O|
C|                                     CLAYTON
U|                         Well, go get cleaned up and we'll 
U|                         proceed with the weddin'...
O|
N|               Charlie frowns and looks off at where Laurie and Martin are 
N|               standing.
O|
C|                                     CHARLIE
U|                         Ain't goin' to be any weddin' -- not 
U|                         till we get a few things cleared up 
U|                         'round here...
O|
N|               He walks rather unsteadily away leaving a thunderstruck 
N|               assembly, murmurous with surprise.
O|
