S,G|               EXT. MESA COUNTRY - LONG SHOT - THE RANGERS - DAWN LIGHT
O|
N,I|               A file of eighteen men and horses -- Rangers -- is walking 
N|               under the shoulder of a mesa, keeping well below the skyline.
O|
G|               FULL SHOT - THE FILE OF RANGERS - DAWN LIGHT
O|
N,G|               They pass CAMERA one by one -- Sam Clayton in the lead, Martin 
N|               behind him leading two horses, then the others -- grim-
N|               looking, capable men of varying ages; some with long drooping 
N|               mustaches, some in need of shaves, some chawing tobacco.
O|
G|               CLOSE SHOT - ETHAN - AT RIM OF A MESA - DAWN LIGHT
O|
N|               He is lying prone, his hat off, squinting down into a long 
N|               reach of desert canyon at the Comanche encampment -- with 
N|               tepees set up, a thin wisp of smoke rising from a fire, the 
N|               horse herd penned in a draw cut off by an improvised corral 
N|               of rawhide ropes.
O|
S,G|               EXT. THE COMANCHE ENCAMPMENT - WIDE ANGLE SHOT - DAWN LIGHT
O|
N|               The camp is sleeping. A dog yaps shrilly. One of the tepee 
N|               flaps opens and Scar steps out. He picks up a stone or a 
N|               chunk of wood and throws it. The dog yelps and runs off. 
N|               Scar's air is troubled, suspicious. He heads for the horse 
N|               herd. The camp sleeps on.
O|
G|               CLOSE SHOT - ETHAN - AT RIM OF A MESA - DAWN LIGHT
O|
N|               His face betrays a bitter inner satisfaction. He looks back 
N|               along the trail as faintly we hear the approach of the Ranger 
N|               company. Then he squirms back, retrieving his hat.
O|
